      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "P_Bc7E_mwjtxjMmohPliP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 273.0403288494691,
      "y": 1962.436127177773,
      "width": 652.6727295777165,
      "height": 383.70290458977513,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "IHNrKEgLtP64vjNb4Wivn"
      ],
      "frameId": "rEX9ZkQmLMonBL9XY3xl",
      "index": "b1YG",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1207104753,
      "version": 279,
      "versionNonce": 109545087,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "oYBcUCmt1vQDnPPbMrUsG",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1782286728189,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Understand the problem and establish design scope (~5 minutes)\nSystem design questions are intentionally vague and open-ended to\ntest how you organize your thoughts [01:36]. Do not jump straight\ninto a solution; instead, ask clarifying questions to establish [01:59]:\n\nFunctional Requirements: Clarify who the users are, why you are\nbuilding the system, and what exact features need to be prioritized\n(e.g., specifying if a chat app is for 1-on-1 WhatsApp-style chats or\nDiscord-style groups) [02:07].\n\nNon-Functional Requirements: Focus primarily on scale and\nperformance [02:48].\n\nBack-of-the-Envelope Calculations: Perform rough mathematical\nestimations to understand the scale, potential bottlenecks, and\norder of magnitude of the system [03:27].",
      "fontSize": 19.185145229488757,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Understand the problem and establish design scope (~5 minutes)\nSystem design questions are intentionally vague and open-ended to test how you organize your thoughts [01:36]. Do not jump straight into a solution; instead, ask clarifying questions to establish [01:59]:\n\nFunctional Requirements: Clarify who the users are, why you are building the system, and what exact features need to be prioritized (e.g., specifying if a chat app is for 1-on-1 WhatsApp-style chats or Discord-style groups) [02:07].\n\nNon-Functional Requirements: Focus primarily on scale and performance [02:48].\n\nBack-of-the-Envelope Calculations: Perform rough mathematical estimations to understand the scale, potential bottlenecks, and order of magnitude of the system [03:27].",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "b2d7sqfRuj6QhF8nW4tOM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1104.8574738424759,
      "y": 1962.4361268694745,
      "width": 934.144640874679,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "IHNrKEgLtP64vjNb4Wivn"
      ],
      "frameId": "rEX9ZkQmLMonBL9XY3xl",
      "index": "b1YV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1442988881,
      "version": 466,
      "versionNonce": 2112904863,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "eWP5J4FTmlw7mVwo3gIvX",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
          "id": "oYBcUCmt1vQDnPPbMrUsG",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1782286728189,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Propose high-level design and get buy-in (~20 minutes)\nDevelop a blueprint for the overall design using a top-down approach [04:02]:\n\nDefine APIs: Establish the contract between the client and the backend using RESTful\nconventions, noting if specialized connections like stateful WebSockets are required [04:09].\n\nHigh-Level Diagram: Map out the client, load balancers, API gateways, and specialized backend\nservices required to achieve the prioritized features [05:16].\n\nData Tier: Round out the design with a data storage layer. Map out the data models,\nschemas, access patterns, and read-to-write ratios. Avoid picking specific database\ntechnologies too early unless it directly solves a critical non-functional constraint [05:44]",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Propose high-level design and get buy-in (~20 minutes)\nDevelop a blueprint for the overall design using a top-down approach [04:02]:\n\nDefine APIs: Establish the contract between the client and the backend using RESTful conventions, noting if specialized connections like stateful WebSockets are required [04:09].\n\nHigh-Level Diagram: Map out the client, load balancers, API gateways, and specialized backend services required to achieve the prioritized features [05:16].\n\nData Tier: Round out the design with a data storage layer. Map out the data models, schemas, access patterns, and read-to-write ratios. Avoid picking specific database technologies too early unless it directly solves a critical non-functional constraint [05:44]",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "hQhswtFktdlq1lLNwddeL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2353.7222962101273,
      "y": 1960.8026249135273,
      "width": 793.3117168044846,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "IHNrKEgLtP64vjNb4Wivn"
      ],
      "frameId": "rEX9ZkQmLMonBL9XY3xl",
      "index": "b1Yl",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 178380511,
      "version": 455,
      "versionNonce": 516502207,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "eWP5J4FTmlw7mVwo3gIvX",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1782286728189,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design deep dive (~15 minutes)\nThis section is highly open-ended and allows you to showcase your senior\nengineering skills by identifying potential problem areas and handling non-\nfunctional requirements [07:21]. The video recommends a mini-guideline for\ndiscussing problems [08:26]:\n\nArticulate the problem: State the exact bottleneck (e.g., 1 million QPS is too\nhigh for a single location database) [08:26].\n\nPropose multiple solutions: Offer at least two options (e.g., reducing update\nfrequency vs. utilizing a NoSQL database) [08:41].\n\nDiscuss trade-offs: Evaluate the pros and cons of your options, backing up your\nclaims with data and numbers [08:57].\n\nPick a solution: Reach an agreement with the interviewer and move on to the\nnext major issue [09:05].",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design deep dive (~15 minutes)\nThis section is highly open-ended and allows you to showcase your senior engineering skills by identifying potential problem areas and handling non-functional requirements [07:21]. The video recommends a mini-guideline for discussing problems [08:26]:\n\nArticulate the problem: State the exact bottleneck (e.g., 1 million QPS is too high for a single location database) [08:26].\n\nPropose multiple solutions: Offer at least two options (e.g., reducing update frequency vs. utilizing a NoSQL database) [08:41].\n\nDiscuss trade-offs: Evaluate the pros and cons of your options, backing up your claims with data and numbers [08:57].\n\nPick a solution: Reach an agreement with the interviewer and move on to the next major issue [09:05].",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
