    {
      "id": "-f1lLY-8JfWauaUMXVY87",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -236.49174922743538,
      "y": 3244.8211721341877,
      "width": 741.5537027744655,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "QOUb4KZXFqglQsoA3RDs",
      "index": "b2Q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1578950015,
      "version": 833,
      "versionNonce": 515545826,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782332969653,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "API (Stateful? Event-Driven?\n    - REST\n        - Default\n        - Prone to under/over fetching\n\n    - GraphQL\n        - choose when diverse clients with different data needs\n        - specific data\n\n    - RPC\n        - User for internal APIs\n\n    - Real-Time\n        0. Webhooks, server<->server\n        1. WebSockets, client<->server, persistent\n        2. Server-Sent Events, client<-server, persistent\n        3. Long Polling, client<-server, closes after each delivery\n\n    - Recent System Design as of Jun 2026 for wearable heartrate devices\nto alert predicted heart attack for 1M users at 200 writes/second\n        1. REST for data ingestion\n        2. RPC for internal inference\n        3. Server-Sent Events for notification",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "API (Stateful? Event-Driven?\n    - REST\n        - Default\n        - Prone to under/over fetching\n\n    - GraphQL\n        - choose when diverse clients with different data needs\n        - specific data\n\n    - RPC\n        - User for itnernal APIs\n\n    - Real-Time\n        0. Webhooks, server<->server\n        1. WebSockets, client<->server, persistent\n        2. Server-Sent Events, client<-server, persistent\n        3. Long Polling, client<-server, closes after each delivery\n\n    - Recent System Design as of Jun 2026 for wearable heartrate devices to alert predicted heart attack for 1M users at 200 writes/second\n        1. REST for data ingestion\n        2. RPC for internal inference\n        3. Server-Sent Events for notification",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
